---

## What I Learned This Week
- Dion practice exams are harder than the real thing — my scores were average 65% on practice but I passed the actual exam. Don't let Dion scores wreck your confidence
- Wireless standards are worth drilling cold: 802.11ac is 5 GHz only, 802.11ax (WiFi 6) is the first to use 6 GHz, 802.11n was the first dual-band standard
- Port memorization is a volume game — repetition over time beats cramming the night before
- Cloud concepts showed up more than expected — worth knowing IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS cold

